  "statement": "A row of `n` beads has colours given by integers. Find the longest block of consecutive beads that uses **at most `k` different colours**, and print its length.\n\n**Input.** First line `n k`. Second line the `n` colours.\n\n**Output.** One integer: the maximum length.\n\n**Example.**\n\nInput:\n```\n7 2\n1 2 1 3 3 3 4\n```\nOutput:\n```\n4\n```",
  "constraints": [
    "1 ≤ n ≤ 1000 in this browser version (the idea scales to 2·10^5)",
    "1 ≤ k ≤ n",
    "1 ≤ colour ≤ 10^9"
  ],
  "timeLimitMs": 1000,
