  "hints": [
    "If a block is valid, is every sub-block of it valid too? What does that suggest about moving the left end?",
    "Grow the window by moving the right end; whenever it has more than `k` colours, advance the left end until valid again.",
    "Keep a map colour -> count. The number of distinct colours is the number of keys with count > 0 (delete keys at 0)."
  ],
  "editorial": "Validity is **monotone under shrinking**: removing beads never adds colours. So for each right end `r`, the set of valid left ends is a suffix `[l(r), r]`, and `l(r)` never decreases as `r` grows (a window ending later that is valid would give a valid shorter window ending earlier). That justifies two pointers: extend `r`, count colours in a map, and while the window has more than `k` colours move `l` right. The answer is the largest `r - l + 1`.\n\nEach pointer moves at most `n` times, so `O(n)` map operations. Forgetting to delete a key when its count hits 0 makes the distinct count wrong.",
  "complexity": {
    "time": "O(n)",
    "space": "O(n)"
  },
  "starter": {
    "python": "import sys\n\n# Longest window with at most k distinct values.\ndata = sys.stdin.read().split()\n# your code here\n",
    "javascript": "// Longest window with at most k distinct values.\n// readLine() returns the next line of input (or null).\n// your code here\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\n\nint main() {\n    // Longest window with at most k distinct values.\n    // your code here\n}\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner in = new Scanner(System.in);\n        // Longest window with at most k distinct values.\n        // your code here\n    }\n}\n"
  },
  "solutions": {
    "python": "import sys\n\ndef main():\n    d = sys.stdin.read().split()\n    n, k = int(d[0]), int(d[1])\n    a = list(map(int, d[2:2 + n]))\n    cnt = {}\n    l = best = 0\n    for r, x in enumerate(a):\n        cnt[x] = cnt.get(x, 0) + 1\n        while len(cnt) > k:          # window invalid: shrink from the left\n            y = a[l]\n            cnt[y] -= 1\n            if cnt[y] == 0:\n                del cnt[y]\n            l += 1\n        best = max(best, r - l + 1)\n    print(best)\n\nmain()\n",
    "javascript": "const __L = [];\nlet __s;\nwhile ((__s = readLine()) !== null) __L.push(__s);\nconst T = __L.join(' ').split(/\\s+/).filter((x) => x.length).map(Number);\nconst n = T[0], k = T[1];\nconst a = T.slice(2, 2 + n);\nconst cnt = new Map();\nlet l = 0, best = 0;\nfor (let r = 0; r < n; r++) {\n  cnt.set(a[r], (cnt.get(a[r]) || 0) + 1);\n  while (cnt.size > k) {\n    const y = a[l];\n    cnt.set(y, cnt.get(y) - 1);\n    if (cnt.get(y) === 0) cnt.delete(y);\n    l++;\n  }\n  best = Math.max(best, r - l + 1);\n}\nconsole.log(String(best));\n",
    "java": "import java.util.*;\nimport java.io.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    static StreamTokenizer st;\n\n    static long nl() throws IOException {\n        st.nextToken();\n        return (long) st.nval;\n    }\n\n    public static void main(String[] args) throws IOException {\n        st = new StreamTokenizer(new BufferedInputStream(System.in));\n        int n = (int) nl(), k = (int) nl();\n        int[] a = new int[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) a[i] = (int) nl();\n        HashMap<Integer, Integer> cnt = new HashMap<>();\n        int l = 0, best = 0;\n        for (int r = 0; r < n; r++) {\n            cnt.merge(a[r], 1, Integer::sum);\n            while (cnt.size() > k) {\n                int y = a[l];\n                int c = cnt.get(y) - 1;\n                if (c == 0) cnt.remove(y);\n                else cnt.put(y, c);\n                l++;\n            }\n            best = Math.max(best, r - l + 1);\n        }\n        System.out.println(best);\n    }\n}\n",
    "cpp": "#include <bits/stdc++.h>\nusing namespace std;\nint main() {\n    int n, k;\n    scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &k);\n    vector<int> a(n);\n    for (auto &v : a) scanf(\"%d\", &v);\n    map<int, int> cnt;\n    int l = 0, best = 0;\n    for (int r = 0; r < n; r++) {\n        cnt[a[r]]++;\n        while ((int)cnt.size() > k) {\n            if (--cnt[a[l]] == 0) cnt.erase(a[l]);\n            l++;\n        }\n        best = max(best, r - l + 1);\n    }\n    printf(\"%d\\n\", best);\n}\n"
  }
